{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792272060,"nonce":"qdpGJWt/fNemKZt0PwZ9upc0wkM=","title":"Wasm module size: what a page-sized program carries and what ash could drop","message":"Reported by the ashui session. An ashui window page built with ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1 and --target wasm32-wasip1-threads on ash 0.1.10+ is 15.16 MB: code 9.97 MB (about 2.5 MB is the ash_std Rust runtime, the rest is compiled Haxe), data 4.73 MB in one segment, name section 0.44 MB. With the other modules the page loads (program, blinc_abi, xgpu, xwindow, ash_browser_bg) it is 24.8 MB raw, 4.9 MB brotli, 6.5 MB gzip.\n\nWhat they tried:\n- ASH_LLVM_PASSES='default\u003cOz\u003e': -3.7% (14.60 MB). 'default\u003cOs\u003e': -1.3%.\n- ASH_AIR_LEVEL=1: +1.7% (larger).\n- Dropping the name section: -0.44 MB.\n- binaryen wasm-opt -Os: -7%, but version 132 emits an import encoding Chrome rejects (\"Invalid import kind 127, enable with --wasm-compact-imports\"), and the output brotli-compresses worse than ash's own.\n\nOnly ash can change, roughly by size:\n1. The single data segment is half zero bytes (2.46 MB of 4.73 MB). A bss-style segment or a memory.fill would remove them from the file.\n2. The runtime links regex_automata (meta::strategy::new alone is 124 KB of code) and the Unicode property tables (script and bidi names are in the data) even when the program uses no EReg. A link-time gate on EReg and on Unicode properties would drop both.\n3. The name section could default to off for wasm builds (0.44 MB on the program, more on side modules).\n4. An --opt-size option, or Oz as the wasm default: one LLVM flag is -3.7%.\n5. The page host ash_browser_bg.wasm is 1.8 MB (1.2 MB without names).\n\nTheir combined recipe (Oz, names dropped, blinc_abi with fat LTO and opt-level z) takes the set to 21 MB raw, 4.4 MB brotli. See ashui docs/web.md and tests/wasm/run.sh (ASHUI_WASM_SMALL=1).\n\nRelated: wasm-module-size-breakdown measured a hello world at 3.96 MB, 96% of it runtime.","files":null}]}